{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0039700","isObsolete":false,"name":"fusion of viral membrane with host outer nuclear membrane","definition":{"text":"Fusion of a viral primary envelope with the host outer nuclear membrane during nuclear egress. The transitory primary envelope is acquired by the virus as it buds at the inner nuclear membrane and gains access to the perinuclear space. This membrane is lost by fusing with the host outer nuclear membrane during nuclear exit.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"23057731"},{"dbCode":"UniProtKB-KW","dbId":"KW-1181"}]},"synonyms":[{"name":"fusion of viral membrane with host outer nuclear membrane involved in nuclear egress","type":"exact"},{"name":"viral primary envelope fusion with host outer nuclear membrane","type":"exact"}],"history":[{"timestamp":"2023-11-01","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2021-11-15","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0016032 (viral process)"},{"timestamp":"2021-11-15","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044800 (obsolete multi-organism membrane fusion)"},{"timestamp":"2015-04-10","action":"Deleted","category":"SYNONYM","text":"viral primary envelope fusion with host outer nuclear membrane"},{"timestamp":"2015-04-10","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"viral primary envelope fusion with host outer nuclear membrane"},{"timestamp":"2013-11-16","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0046802 (exit of virus from host cell nucleus by nuclear egress)"},{"timestamp":"2013-11-16","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0039676 (exit of virus from host cell nucleus by nuclear egress)"},{"timestamp":"2013-11-08","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044800 (obsolete multi-organism membrane fusion)"},{"timestamp":"2013-11-08","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0039676 (exit of virus from host cell nucleus by nuclear egress)"},{"times